

= Appendix : Contextual Inquiry

== Interview Question (Founder)

*Introduction*
1. Could you briefly describe your respective roles in relation to RehAtt® DiSTRO and the XR rehabilitation games?
2. Could you give a brief overview of your research history in visuospatial neglect and VR-based rehabilitation? Followup: Why did you start Brain Stimulation
3. Looking back, what key insights from your early research most strongly shaped the initial design of RehAtt and the decision to use VR and XR technologies for VSN rehabilitation? Why XR?
4. Without XR, how is the rehabilitation currently performed?

*Product*
5. How are the current tests for Distro selected? What are the criterias for new tests selected?
6. There was references (compare to examples) in Distro? What are those examples based on?
7. What cognitive or perceptual aspects of visuospatial neglect do the current tests aim to capture? Are some aspects intentionally prioritized over others?
8. Were there any constructs you wanted to measure but had to exclude due to technical or clinical constraints?

*Assessment and Exergames*
9. What is the use case difference between physiotherapists and Ots using this product? 
10. Similarly, how are the games selected for XR? 
11. How do therapists currently use the assessment results to decide which rehabilitation games to use and at what difficulty level?
12. Which assessment results are most influential when tailoring therapy for a patient with VSN? Follow-up: Are some results underused or harder to interpret?
13. To what extent is this decision-making standardized versus dependent on individual therapist expertise?
14. Are there aspects of a patient’s visuospatial neglect or recovery that are difficult to capture with the current assessment tools?  Prompt: behavior, fatigue, attention, asymmetries, strategy use
16. From your experience, where do therapists struggle most when translating assessment data into individualized rehabilitation? Like: time, confidence, lack of controls, lack of granularity
16. What makes levels harder/simpler, what is the logic behind the levels? is it related to research as well or not?
17. In an ideal system, how much control should be manual versus automatically adaptive?

*General*
18. In an ideal system, how much control should be manual versus automatically adaptive?
19. Over the years of deploying RehAtt and DiSTRO, what have been the biggest surprises—either in how therapists use the systems or how patients respond to XR-based rehabilitation?
20. If you were redesigning the therapist-facing control layer around the XR games today, what would you do differently based on what you now know?
21. Is there anything we didn’t ask that you think is critical when designing future XR-based rehabilitation systems for VSN?

== Interview Questions (Product Owner)
*Introduction*
1. Could you briefly describe your respective roles in relation to RehAtt® DiSTRO and the XR rehabilitation games?	
2. From your perspective, what are the primary clinical use cases and target user groups?

*Walkthrough with DiSTRO*
3. Can you walk us through how RehAtt® DiSTRO is typically used in practice, from assessment start to results
4. What cognitive or perceptual aspects of visuospatial neglect do the current tests aim to capture? Are some aspects intentionally prioritized over others? Why?
5. What are the tests that are currently in the system? or are in plans? Why is there a need to add more tasks?
6. How were the specific tasks(tests) selected and translated into digital form?
7. What kind of metrics does the assessment generate for therapists today from DISTRO? Are any other sources also included in this? (Scores, Information Visualizations, Trends over time)
8. When multiple assessments are performed, are they shown as a trend in the system or do OTs infer it from the separate cognitive assessment reports? 
9. You have a disclaimer saying “test availability may differ depending on region” regarding the distro platform on your website, could you elaborate on why that is?

*Walkthrough with XR Remote*
10. Can you walk us through the XR Remote and how it is intended for therapists to use it?
11. What are the controls that are provided to the therapists?
12. What makes levels harder/simpler, what is the logic behind the levels? is it related to research as well or not?
13. How were the XR game tasks and mechanics chosen to align with the assessment from DiSTRO, if at all?

*General*
14. In an ideal system, how much control should be manual versus automatically adaptive?
15. From a technical and product perspective, what limits or constraints have you seen that has affected the adaptability of games? Like: safety, regulation, usability, development complexity
16. Have therapists requested any new features or controls for DiSTRO or the XR games that have not yet been implemented? If so, which ones and why have they not been prioritized or released yet?
17. Have you done any internal or external studies on how therapists use these tools (e.g., usability tests, field feedback), and what were the key findings that influenced product decisions?
18. Is there anything we didn’t ask that you think is critical when designing future XR-based rehabilitation systems for VSN?


== Interview Questions (Occuptational Therapists)

*Introduction*
1. Could you briefly describe your role? And how long you have been professionally working as an occupational therapist? 
2. How often do you work with patients who have VSN or similar difficulties? (visual scanning / attention) 
3. What are your main goals when planning and delivering rehabilitaiton sessions for the patients? 

*Current Use Experience (Likes/Dislikes)* 
4. Do you (or have you) used digital technologies to provide rehabilitation?  
  If yes, how long have you used technology (Distro, RehattXR or other XR technology) to provide rehabilitation to stroke patients or any patient with cognitive or motor issues? 
5. What kinds of assessments/training do you currently use to understand a patient’s VSN and related cognitive or perceptual difficulties? (Paper, Standardised Tools, Digital Tools, etc) 
6. How difficult/easy to use do you find the tool Distro / RehattXR to be and why? 
    a. What are the main pain points?  
    b. What would you like to see instead? 
7. How difficult/easy was the learning curve of the tool Distro/RehattXR and what do you think may have caused it? 
8. From your experience, where do therapists struggle most when translating assessment data into individualized rehabilitation? Prompt: time, confidence, lack of controls, lack of granularity 

*Assessment and Information *
9. What specific information do you pay most attention to when planning and performing therapy? 
10. How do you provide assessment data or analysis to the OTs that perform rehab processes? OR How do you receive assessment data or report from OTs that perform the assessment of the patient? 
11. If any, what aspects of a patient’s visuospatial neglect or recovery do find to be difficult to capture with the current assessment tools?  Like : behavior, fatigue, attention, asymmetries, strategy use 
 

*Controls/ During & After Sessions *
12. We saw that you can control levels 1-70. What additional controls would you want to be able to manipulate and why? 
13. Are there situations where you would prefer the system to automatically adapt to difficulty, and situations where you would insist on manual control? 
14. What parts of the rehabilitation training do you want to be able to control. If a rehabliitaiton session is divdied into phases: pre-training, during training and post-training, what level of controls do you want in each phase?  Or if you want it to be divided into different phases that is fine too.  
15. Do you want more controls in how the sessions is configured in the digtial system or less controls? How much time are you realistically willing to spend configuring or adjusting a digital task before or during a session? 

*Future / Missing Features * 
16. What additional features is important for you to have that you yet don’t have in the platforms RehattXR?
    Could you explain why they are important and how they could help you in your assessment and in providing more personalized rehabilitation? 
17. As we have understood, you use cognitive screening/repeated training in RehattXR to understand patients' attention, memory and motor limitations, do you feel like there is anything within or outside those areas that are missing?  
18. If you could redesign the assessment–therapy connection from scratch today, what could a well-designed XR or digital system enable you during VSN rehabilitation? 
19. Is there anything we didn’t ask that you think is critical when designing a future control system for XR-based rehabilitation for VSN? 

